<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · period</p><h1 class="enc-title">Middle Bronze Age</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 2000–1550 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century-bce">21st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> is the archaeological period of roughly 2000 to 1550 BCE in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>. Canaanite towns revived and grew into fortified cities surrounded by massive earth ramparts and sloping glacis, as at Acco, Lachish, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashkelon">Ashkelon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. Many appear in Egyptian execration texts, and the period ended with the Egyptian campaigns that followed the expulsion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyksos">Hyksos</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/middle-bronze-age.jpg" alt="Middle Bronze Age" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Want · CC BY-SA 3.0 cz · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Metallurgical_diffusion.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
